  "settings.myskoda.heading": "Automatic Charging Detection (MyŠkoda Public API)",
  "settings.myskoda.description": "A second source, independent of Home Assistant, for automatically detected charging sessions: the server queries the official <a href=\"https://public.api.connect.skoda-auto.cz/docs\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">MyŠkoda Public API</a> itself and creates detected charging sessions (always flagged as \"needs review\"). The existing Home Assistant push keeps running in parallel, unchanged – the two sources are unaware of each other, so duplicate sessions must be avoided by keeping only one path active per vehicle.<br><br>Create an API key at <a href=\"https://go.skoda.eu/api-keys\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">go.skoda.eu/api-keys</a> (open the link on your phone, the MyŠkoda app manages the keys). The key is bound to the vehicles selected when it was created and expires after some time – the expiry date is shown below once a request has been made.<br><br><strong>Rate limit: 20 requests per hour per API key</strong>, shared across all vehicles and clients. If the Home Assistant integration runs in parallel with the same key, both share this quota – in that case, creating a second key is recommended. The default intervals (20 min idle, 5 min during a charging session) stay comfortably below that.<br><br><strong>Accuracy:</strong> the start of charging is only noticed on the next poll, so the initial SoC tends to be a bit too high and the estimated energy a bit too low – negligible for AC charging, not for DC fast charging. Every detected session gets a note with the before/after values so the error can be traced.",
